From ab6296dc8068f0686111af1b4810530574162233 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aarya Parekh <aarya@local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 03:42:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] =?UTF-8?q?perf+refactor:=20Kyle=20O(1)=20R=C2=B2,=20c?=
 =?UTF-8?q?onsolidate=20profiler,=20dead-code=20cleanup?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

perf:
- kyle_lambda: R² and t-stat via closed-form on centered sums, not by
  rescanning the sliding window every tick. Same output to FP noise
  (max abs diff 4.4e-15 over 5000 ticks); 16× faster on the Kyle module
  in local benchmark. Removes a hidden O(n) inside a docstring that
  claimed O(1) per-tick.
- spread.weighted_spread: single pass per side instead of three.
- models.OrderBookSnapshot.midprice: index bids/asks directly rather
  than routing through the best_bid/best_ask properties.

refactor:
- profiler now runs the same _run_modules pipeline as Engine with a
  timing hook, instead of a hand-copied duplicate of Engine.process.
  Eliminates two parallel metrics-dict builders that had to be kept in
  sync manually. Adding a signal in engine.py now flows through the
  profiler automatically.
- SymbolAnalytics gets __slots__; ProfiledSymbolAnalytics deleted
  (was verbatim dup).
- Engine._get uses .get() to skip the double dict lookup on the hot path.

dead code removed:
- OrderBookSnapshot.spread property (no callers; spread.quoted_spread
  is the actual API).
- VolumeProfile.cum_delta backward-compat alias (nothing calls it —
  all references are to the cumulative_delta property or to the
  cum_delta *metrics-dict key*, which is different).
- Redundant 'if self._prev_x else 0.0' guards in kyle_lambda and
  hasbrouck (the enclosing guard already ensures prev is a positive
  float).

docs:
- README: restore Codacy/SonarCloud badges pointing at the current repo
  name, with a note that the dashboards themselves may need renaming.

verified:
- Engine and ProfiledEngine produce byte-identical metrics dicts on a
  500-tick synthetic stream.
- Kyle output identical to pre-refactor (max FP diff 4.44e-15).
