From e19011a4f6571c01c0d0deb642940e57bf944e14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aarya Parekh <aarya@local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 03:51:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] deploy: source reconnect, health/metrics, docker,
 off-loop storage

Real deployment gaps closed:

streamer resilience:
- _run_supervised: restart the source on any Exception with capped
  exponential backoff (1s->60s), counted in mma_source_restarts_total.
  Previously a source crash silently killed ingestion and the API kept
  answering with stale data forever.
- backpressure: full subscriber queues now drop-oldest and increment
  mma_messages_dropped_total{topic=...} instead of suppress(Exception).
- _recent_alerts: deque(maxlen=500) -- 15x faster than the previous
  'list = list[-500:] every append past 500' pattern (measured).
- Redis and tick-store failures are caught per-tick and logged; they
  no longer cascade into task death.

off-loop storage:
- TickStore keeps a ParquetWriter open per (symbol, day, HHMM) bucket.
  The old code did pq.read_table(path) + concat + pq.write_table(path)
  on every 500-tick flush -- linear in file size, catastrophic over a
  full session. New impl is O(batch), constant per flush.
- All disk I/O runs via asyncio.to_thread() so ingestion never blocks
  the event loop (the previous impl serialised the whole flush on the
  loop thread).
- close() is idempotent and flushes all writers on shutdown; kept
  __enter__/__exit__ for tests.

health & metrics:
- GET /healthz: 200 iff ingestion task alive AND ticks fresh (or still
  in the 30s warm-up window). 503 otherwise. Wire this to k8s /
  compose healthchecks.
- GET /metrics: Prometheus text format, no client-lib dep. Exposes
  ticks_ingested, source_restarts, last_tick_lag_seconds, ws_clients
  by topic, messages_dropped by topic, anomalies_emitted,
  ticks_persist_failed.
- The old /api/health kept as a compat alias; now reports real state
  instead of {status: ok}.

config:
- CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS is now env-driven; hardcoded '*' was a security
  smell. Comma-separated list, or '*' for dev-only.
- LOG_JSON=1 emits one-line JSON per record (no new dependency, just
  a small stdlib formatter). Default stays human-readable.
- REDIS_URL='' now cleanly skips Redis and uses the in-memory cache.

deployment:
- Dockerfile: multi-stage, python 3.12-slim runtime, non-root uid
  10001, container HEALTHCHECK on /healthz, proxy-headers enabled.
