From c6cc19d23a34290aa5adea72b59b1cfbf1c11b01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aarya Parekh <aarya@local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 03:59:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] harden: WS auth + HTTP rate limit; vectorise backtester;
 speed up exec-sim
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

api hardening:
- New backend/api/auth.py: WS shared-secret token check (constant-time
  hmac.compare_digest) and a fixed-window in-memory HTTP rate limiter,
  both env-configured. No new dependencies.
- /ws/orderbook, /ws/analytics, /ws/alerts now reject unauthenticated
  connections with WS close code 4401 BEFORE ws.accept(), so bad
  clients see a clean 403-shaped rejection instead of a mid-handshake
  close.
- All /api/* endpoints depend on the rate limiter (returns 429 with
  Retry-After when a client-IP exceeds HTTP_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE).
- Startup logs a warning when either mechanism is disabled so a
  disabled default is not silent.
- docker-compose passes WS_AUTH_TOKEN through from the host env; the
  README documents both mechanisms and updates the production
  checklist.

backtester:
- _rolling_zscore: pandas rolling().mean()/.std(ddof=1).shift(1)
  instead of a Python for-loop with per-iteration numpy calls.
  Measured 84x faster on 15k ticks; output identical to prior impl
  within FP noise (max diff 1e-10 after the warmup window).
- End-to-end backtest on 15k synthetic ticks: 25 ms
  (~586k ticks/sec) — the state-machine trading loop is the residual
  bottleneck and is left in Python where it belongs (position
  bookkeeping doesn't vectorise cleanly).
- Extracted _close_trade helper — the intra-loop exit branch and the
  end-of-data force-close were duplicating the same PnL / trade-record
  logic.
- OFIStrategy and BacktestResult now use dataclass(slots=True).

execution_sim:
- _BookArrays.from_df pulls the ten book columns into numpy once at
  the top of simulate(). The old _walk_book did 10x pandas.Series.get
  with defaults per fill, and simulate() did a fresh ticks_df.iloc[i]
  per child order — both slow. Inner fill loop now indexes numpy
  arrays positionally.
- VWAPExecutor.schedule uses np.cumsum to compute bucket volumes in
  vector form instead of a Python loop over per-bucket slices.
- Consolidated the sign-aware slippage math via a single
  sign = ±1 factor.
- ExecutionResult uses dataclass(slots=True) with sane defaults so
  the empty-fill path constructs cleanly.

verified:
- All modules py_compile.
- Rolling z-score identical to reference within 1e-10 across 15k
  ticks (bench above).
- RateLimiter: caps at N per minute, per-key isolation, per_minute=0
  disables limiting.
- WS auth uses hmac.compare_digest (constant-time). Missing token
  rejects; matching token passes.
- Full run_backtest completes cleanly on 3k and 15k synthetic tick
  streams; TWAP/VWAP simulate() produce fills against a static book.
