From: Aarya Parekh <aarya@local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 04:13:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] tests+perf: 34 tests for deploy surface; fix
 sync-Redis-on-loop; kill asdict per-tick
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

perf fixes:

state_cache: put_snapshot_async runs the Redis network call on a
  thread (asyncio.to_thread). The Streamer._handle now uses this
  variant so a slow Redis never stalls the event loop. In-memory
  backend skips the thread detour (bare dict set is faster inline).

_serialize_snapshot no longer calls dataclasses.asdict. asdict
  recursively deep-copies every nested BookLevel through Python
  function calls; hand-building the dict was measured 4.3x faster
  end-to-end (json.dumps included): 79 us/tick -> 18 us/tick on a
  5-level book. Same on-the-wire shape; timezone-aware ts
  serialised via .isoformat() as before.

tests (34 new, all in-process, no external deps):

backend/tests/test_streamer.py (13):
- is_healthy: warming_up ok, task-dead not ok, stale not ok, fresh ok
- source reconnect: crashing-then-recovering source triggers exactly
  one restart and all ticks land
- backoff supervisor: repeated crashes drive source_restarts_total
  upward within a bounded time window
- clean source end: no restart when stream returns cleanly
- ticks_ingested counter tracks a synthetic 25-tick source
- _broadcast: full queue drops oldest AND increments the
  messages_dropped counter (regression test for the previous silent
  suppress-Exception bug)
- deque(maxlen=500) enforces the alerts bound; recent_alerts(limit)
  semantics
- ws_clients gauge tracks sub/unsub correctly
- _anomaly_to_dict isoformats the timestamp

backend/tests/test_storage.py (9):
- append then read_day roundtrip; column order
- bucket rotation: timestamps spanning a 15-minute boundary write to
  separate parquet files (0900.parquet vs 0915.parquet)
- close() is idempotent — safe on shutdown
- context-manager __exit__ closes and flushes
- reopen an existing bucket file preserves history (rehydrates the
  first row group so process restart is safe)
- flush_every trigger writes without needing close()
- state_cache._serialize_snapshot shape check
- StateCache in-memory sync roundtrip
- StateCache.put_snapshot_async in-memory path

backend/tests/test_api_deploy.py (12):
- /healthz returns 200 during warm-up, 503 when ticks stale, 503
  when the ingestion task is dead
- /metrics: content-type text/plain, HELP+TYPE preambles for every
  metric, values landed for counters and labelled gauges/counters
- /api/* endpoints served when rate-limit disabled
- /api/* returns 429 with Retry-After header when the per-IP cap
  trips; RateLimiter itself: per-key isolation, per_minute=0
  disables entirely
- WS: dev-mode (no token) accepts; wrong token closes with 4401;
  correct token accepts; missing token when required closes with
  4401 (all four endpoints checked)

fixtures monkeypatch the streamer singleton with a fresh instance so
tests don't share process-level state (metrics, subscribers, buckets).

verified:
- All modules py_compile.
- Hand-serialise output byte-identical to old asdict path.
- asyncio_mode='auto' is already set in pyproject.toml, so
  @pytest.mark.asyncio is not needed on the async tests.
